// rustc moves/issue-75904-move-closure-loop.rs — upstream E0382 use of moved value
// imported batch B167 @ da5114692c9ebe46b869488c5f34f92eb10b98c1 (rust 1.100.0)
// shelf: admit · root nllmoves.C — RE-PORTED AS-IS 2026-09-07 (stage 4)
// ── BUCKET 3: BLESSED DIVERGENCE, docs/DIVERGENCES.md A16 (structural auto-Copy,
//    canonised by Victor 2026-08-24). NOT A BORROW-CHECK DEFECT.
//    Upstream's `struct NotCopy;` is field-less and carries no `impl Drop`, so under
//    A16 ("implicitly Copy iff no `impl Drop` AND every field type is Copy" — vacuous
//    for a field-less struct) it IS Copy here, and `let m = a;` is a COPY. The program
//    is LEGAL Logos as written. Row moved to bc_admits_blocked.ledger.
//    MEASURED ONE-VARIABLE PAIR, 2026-09-07 — the ONLY difference is the `impl Drop`:
//      struct NotCopy;                          + `loop { || { let m = a; }; }`  ADMITS
//      struct NotCopy{z:i64} impl Drop for ..   + the same loop body              REFUSES
//        "error [fn main]: use of moved value 'a' (moved on line 6)"
//    So the closure-in-a-loop move IS checked; only this port's TYPE is Copy. Swapping
//    the type would change the subject, which is why this is bucket 3 and not a re-port.
// Original path: tests/ui/moves/issue-75904-move-closure-loop.rs
// upstream commit: 4b0c9d76ae7d387229caea55cfa73c280b08b8a7
// upstream construct: lines 7-14 —
//     let mut a = NotCopy;
//     loop { || { //~ ERROR use of moved value
//         &mut a;
//         a;
//     }; }
// Modifications:
//   · assert -> exit code: `fn main() -> i32`. NOTHING ELSE — the type, the `loop`, the
//     closure, the `&mut a` and the by-value `a` are upstream's, verbatim.
package issue_75904_move_closure_loop;
struct NotCopy;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut a: NotCopy = NotCopy;
    loop {
        || { let r = &mut a; let m = a; };
    }
}
